You are a Architect, your goal is design a concise, usable, complete software system. the constraint is make sure the architecture is simple enough and use appropriate open source libraries.
Aim to achieve functional requirements, only require to implement demo.
If the original requirements have data storage requirements, you need to design a simple data storage method for the software. Do not use SQL datasets. Follow the data storage requirements in the software requirements(including data format, storage requirements, etc.).


## Context
original_requirement
# Software Description

## Objective
Develop a comprehensive web application named 'RemoteJobBoard' that allows users to browse, post, and manage remote job listings. Note that the website should start from the login page.


## Core Features

Users shall be able to log in using their username and password on the login page.
Users shall be able to navigate to the registration page to create a new account.
Users shall be able to input a username and password to create a new account on the registration page.
Users shall be able to navigate to the home page after successful login.
Users shall be able to view featured job listings on the home page.
Users shall be able to browse all job listings by clicking on a "Browse Jobs" button.
Users shall be able to post a new job listing by navigating to the job posting page.
Users shall be able to edit their profile by navigating to the profile page.
Users shall be able to apply for specific job postings on the job listings page.
Authorized users shall be able to post a new job by entering job details, such as job title, company name, and job description.
Users shall be able to view their profile, which displays their username, email, applied job list, and options to edit their profile.
Users shall be able to log out from the application via the logout button on the profile page.

## Language

Use html and python to develop a web application.
You should use html to generate the web template by yourself.
## Data Storage
Data will be stored in local text files.
Different types of data will be stored in separate `.txt` files.
You should define the text file by yourself in advance.
This structured data storage will facilitate easy data retrieval and management through simple file manipulations in Python, ensuring the application remains light and efficient without the need for a SQL database.
functional requirements
[OUTPUT]
## general overview of the project
Develop a comprehensive web application named 'RemoteJobBoard' that allows users to browse, post, and manage remote job listings. Note that the website should start from the login page.
## software functional requirements
1. Users shall be able to log in using their username and password on the login page.
2. Users shall be able to navigate to the registration page to create a new account.
3. Users shall be able to input a username and password to create a new account on the registration page.
4. Users shall be able to navigate to the home page after successful login.
5. Users shall be able to view featured job listings on the home page.
6. Users shall be able to browse all job listings by clicking on a "Browse Jobs" button.
7. Users shall be able to post a new job listing by navigating to the job posting page.
8. Users shall be able to edit their profile by navigating to the profile page.
9. Users shall be able to apply for specific job postings on the job listings page.
10. Authorized users shall be able to post a new job by entering job details, such as job title, company name, and job description.
11. Users shall be able to view their profile, which displays their username, email, applied job list, and options to edit their profile.
12. Users shall be able to log out from the application via the logout button on the profile page.
[/OUTPUT]

## lessons and experience
### Overall Evaluation
- **Strengths:**
  - Flask is effectively utilized for rapid and lightweight application development.
  - Clear separation of responsibilities in `UserManager` and `JobManager` classes enhances functionality management.
  - Simple HTML templates facilitate user interaction and navigation, focusing on essential tasks like login, registration, and job posting.

- **Weaknesses:**
  - The UI lacks advanced features such as job filtering, sorting, and search capabilities, which can hinder user experience.
  - Data storage through text files may lead to management challenges and questions of data integrity as complexity grows.

### Specific Problems and Suggestions
- **UI Enhancement:**
  - Implement job filtering (by title, company) and sorting options (by date) to improve navigation.
  - Introduce a dedicated job detail page with comprehensive job information and an application form.

- **User Feedback:**
  - Provide inline confirmation messages for actions like job postings and applications to keep users informed.
  - Implement basic error handling and validation for user inputs (e.g., during registration and job postings) to enhance user experience.

- **Data Management:**
  - Introduce a logging mechanism to track application statuses (e.g., pending, accepted, rejected) and user actions within the application.

- **Concurrency Issues:**
  - Consider implementing file-locking mechanisms or using in-memory data structures to manage concurrent accesses and prevent data inconsistencies.

### Architecture Enhancements
- **Implementation Structure:**
  - Continue leveraging Flask but consider using Blueprints to organize the application into distinct modules (e.g., user management, job management). This separation can enhance maintainability.

- **UI Improvements:**
  - Add interactive elements like a search bar for job keywords and filters for job types, enhancing user engagement.
  - Ensure the UI is responsive and accessible across various devices, potentially utilizing frameworks like Bootstrap.

- **Data Storage Optimization:**
  - Expand the data model to include additional fields in user and job records (e.g., job requirements, application history) for more comprehensive management.
  - Consider creating a dedicated file (e.g., `applications.txt`) to manage job application logs and statuses clearly.

- **Refinement of Data Structures:**
  - Ensure the `UserManager` and `JobManager` classes adhere to the Single Responsibility Principle and encapsulate all related logic efficiently.

By addressing these suggestions and improvements, the RemoteJobBoard application can enhance its functionality, user experience, and overall architecture, making it more robust and scalable for future developments.

